    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Surgical Orthodontics by Dr Dante Gonzales | Expert Jaw Alignment Care"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "When teeth and jaws don’t meet as they should, regular braces alone may not be enough. This is where surgical orthodontics comes in. At Dr Dante Gonzales Orthodontics, we work closely with many experienced oral and maxillofacial surgeons to correct severe jaw irregularities and bring the face back into balance. Feels like real precision work sometimes."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "That interrupted sleep may seem harmless but it isn’t. It can raise high blood pressure, lead to cardiovascular issues and affect your whole health and daily energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Book a Surgical Orthodontic Consultation",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "dublin-ca-orthodontic-office-contact.php",
          "text": "Book a Surgical Orthodontic Consultation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Surgical Orthodontics: When Braces Alone Aren’t Enough"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Surgical orthodontics, also known as orthognathic surgery, is a part of the nine recognized dental specialties. It combines jaw surgery with orthodontic treatment to fix improper bites, misaligned jaws, or serious facial aesthetic concerns."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It’s a major medical surgery but done with great planning and accuracy. The surgical procedure adjusts the upper and lower jaws to restore proper alignment and improve both jaw function and facial symmetry. We offer surgical orthodontics for adults and older teens whose jaw growth is finished."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "That’s how we see it anyway, timing matters more than anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "assets/brand/logo-mark.png",
      "alt": "Logo",
      "title": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Want to know if you’re a candidate for braces or Invisalign?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Take Our 30-Second Quiz Now To Find Out!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Take Quiz Now!",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "invisalign-quiz.php",
          "text": "Take Quiz Now!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Who Needs Surgical Orthodontics and Why"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Our team may recommend orthognathic surgery if the patient has:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Difficulty chewing or biting"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Improper bites or open bites"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Noticeable jaw bone abnormalities"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Facial appearance imbalance"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Breathing or speech issues related to jaw position"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "These are often complex craniofacial cases. Treating them means coordinating between the surgical orthodontist and maxillofacial surgeon. Together they create a precise treatment plan that addresses both function and aesthetic concerns."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Meet Our Surgical Orthodontist Today",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "dublin-ca-orthodontic-office-contact.php",
          "text": "Meet Our Surgical Orthodontist Today"
        }
      ]
    },
